/07/brie-larson-kong-skull-island-1201483997/ |access-date=July 27, 2015 |website=Deadline Hollywood |date=July 23, 2015 |archive-date=July 27, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150727002803/http://deadline.com/2015/07/brie-larson-kong-skull-island-1201483997/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On August 5, 2015, it was announced that Corey Hawkins joined the cast in a supporting role.<ref name="HawkinsCast" /> In August 2015, ''[[Deadline Hollywood]]'' reported that the studio was in early talks with [[Samuel L. Jackson]] to replace the role Simmons vacated, while [[John C. Reilly]] was eyed for Keaton's role but not offered it yet. [[Tom Wilkinson]] was offered a role in the film.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Fleming |first1=Mike Jr. |title=Is There Room On 'Kong: Skull Island' For Samuel L. Jackson And Tom Wilkinson? |url=https://deadline.com/2015/08/kong-skull-island-samuel-l-jackson-tom-wilkinson-1201493619/ |access-date=August 7, 2015 |website=Deadline Hollywood |date=August 6, 2015 |archive-date=August 9, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150809012628/http://deadline.com/2015/08/kong-skull-island-samuel-l-jackson-tom-wilkinson-1201493619/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

In August 2015, [[Toby Kebbell]] joined the film's cast, while Jackson and Reilly were confirmed for roles.<ref name="KebbellCast">{{cite web |last=Kit |first=Borys |title='Fantastic Four' Actor Toby Kebbell Joins Tom Hiddleston in 'Kong: Skull Island' (Exclusive) |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/fantastic-four-actor-toby-kebbell-816450 |access-date=August 21, 2015 |work=The Hollywood Reporter |date=August 20, 2015 |archive-date=August 23, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150823001237/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/fantastic-four-actor-toby-kebbell-816450 |url-status=live }}</ref> Jackson's deal was worth five million dollars.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/features/how-samuel-l-jackson-became-hollywoods-bankable-star-1174613 |title=120 Movies, $13 Billion in Box Office: How Samuel L. Jackson Became Hollywood's Most Bankable Star |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |date=January 9, 2019 |access-date=January 9, 2019 |archive-date=May 10, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190510121204/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/features/how-samuel-l-jackson-became-hollywoods-bankable-star-1174613 |url-status=live }}</ref> In August 2015, [[Jason Mitchell]] joined the cast to play a pilot.<ref name="MitchellCast">{{cite web |last=Kroll |first=Justin |title='Straight Outta Compton's' Jason Mitchell Joins Legendary's 'Skull Island' |url=https://variety.com/2015/film/news/straight-outta-comptons-jason-mitchell-joins-legendarys-skull-island-1201578378/ |access-date=August 26, 2015 |work=Variety |date=August 25, 2015 |archive-date=August 26, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150826181716/http://variety.com/2015/film/news/straight-outta-comptons-jason-mitchell-joins-legendarys-skull-island-1201578378/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In September 2015, [[John Goodman]] was cast to play Randa, a government official and leader of an expedition and [[Thomas Mann (actor)|Thomas Mann]] was also cast.