e-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151017045630/http://deadline.com/2015/10/eugene-cordero-kong-skull-island-amiah-miller-war-for-the-planet-of-the-apes-1201579832/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In November 2015, it was announced that [[Will Brittain]] had joined the cast, portraying a pilot, in one of the last key leads in the film.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/will-brittain-kong-skull-island-836118 |title='Kong: Skull Island' Casts Up-And-Comer for Pilot Role |work=The Hollywood Reporter |first=Borys |last=Kit |date=November 2, 2015 |access-date=November 2, 2015 |archive-date=November 5, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151105222015/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/will-brittain-kong-skull-island-836118 |url-status=live }}</ref> In May 2016, Toby Kebbell revealed that [[Terry Notary]] would perform Kong through motion capture and that Kebbell provided some guidance for Kong's motion capture sequences.<ref name="ew11" />

===Filming===
[[Principal photography]] on the film began on October 19, 2015, and concluded on March 18, 2016.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.instagram.com/p/BDFTAQLDI-r/  |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/s/instagram/BDFTAQLDI-r |archive-date=December 26, 2021 |url-access=registration|title=That's a wrap. 📷 by @tutututuuuu |publisher=[[Instagram.com]] |first=Thomas |last=Mann |date=March 18, 2016 |access-date=March 20, 2016}}{{cbignore}}</ref> Filming took place in the northern portion of [[Vietnam]], including [[Tràng An Scenic Landscape Complex|Tràng An]], Vân Long and [[Tam Cốc-Bích Động|Tam Cốc]] ([[Ninh Bình Province]]), [[Hạ Long Bay]] ([[Quảng Ninh Province]]), and the entrance of [[Tú Làn Caves System]] (Tân Hoá, Trung Hoá Village, Minh Hoá District [[Quảng Bình Province]]) with the help of The Creatv Company in Vietnam and [[Nicholas Simon]] as line producer.<ref>{{cite news|last= Scarpinato|first= John|date= March 9, 2017|title= On Location: Director Jordan Vogt-Roberts on Filming 'Kong: Skull Island' in Vietnam|url= https://www.travelandleisure.com/trip-ideas/kong-skull-island-vietnam|work= Travel + Leisure|location= |access-date= March 30, 2021|archive-date= February 26, 2021|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20210226221732/https://www.travelandleisure.com/trip-ideas/kong-skull-island-vietnam|url-status= live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last= Brzeski|first= Patrick|date= May 18, 2017|title= Cannes: IndoChina Head Talks 'A Prayer Before Dawn' and Shooting in Southeast Asia|url= https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/cannes-indochina-head-talks-a-prayer-before-dawn-shooting-southeast-asia-1004989|work= The Hollywood Reporter|location= |access-date= March 30, 2021|archive-date= March 4, 2021|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20210304200713/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/cannes-indochina-head-talks-a-prayer-before-dawn-shooting-southeast-asia-1004989|url-status= live}}</ref>

Filming also took place on the island of Oahu in Hawaii, with Renee Confair as production supervisor,<ref>{{cite web |url= https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0174553/?ref_=ttfc_fc_cr125|title= Renee Confair|author=<!--Not stated--> |date= |website= IMDb|access-date= March 30, 2021}}</ref> and Australia's Gold Coast, with Jennifer Cornwell as production manager for the unit.<ref>{{cite web |url= https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0180496/?ref_=ttfc_fc_cr110|title= Jennifer Cornwell|author=<!--Not stated--> |date= |website= IMDb|access-date= March 30, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.ausfilm.com.au/what-we-do/campaigns/wizards-of-oz/jennifer-cornwell/|title= Wizards of Oz: Jennifer Cornwell|author= <!--Not stated-->|date= |website= Ausfilm|access-date= March 30, 2021|archive-date= April 18, 2021|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20210418171300/https://www.ausfilm.com.au/what-we-do/campaigns/wizards-of-oz/jennifer-cornwell/|url-status= live}}</ref> Locations included [[Chinatown, Honolulu|Honolulu's Chinatown]] and the [[Kualoa Ranch]] and Waikane Valley (Ohulehule Forest Conservancy) on [[Oahu]].<ref>{{cite web |title='Kong: Skull Island' spotted filming at Kualoa Ranch in Hawaii |url=http://www.onlocationvacations.com/2015/10/23/kong-skull-island-spotted-filming-at-kualoa-ranch-in-hawaii/ |access-date=October 26, 2015 |work=On Location Vacations |date=October 23, 2015 |archive-date=October 24, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151024165154/http://www.onlocationvacations.com/2015/10/23/kong-skull-island-spotted-filming-at-kualoa-ranch-in-hawaii/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Gordon |first=Mike |title=King Kong movie filming closes Chinatown streets |url=http://www.staradvertiser.com/traffic/portion-of-king-street-in-chinatown-will-be-closed-for-film-shoot/ |newspaper=[[Honolulu Star-Advertiser|StarAdvertiser]] |location=Honolulu |date=December 17, 2015 |access-date=December 17, 2015 |archive-date=March 4, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304134840/http://www.staradvertiser.com/traffic/p-ortion-of-king-street-in-chinatown-will-be-closed-for-film-shoot/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In mid-January 2016, filming started in the [[Gold Coast, Queensland|Gold Coast]], [[Queensland]], Australia.<ref>{{cite web |title='Kong: Skull Island' moves from Hawaii to Australia |url=http://www.onlocationvacations.com/2016/01/20/kong-skull-island-moves-hawaii-australia/ |access-date=January 26, 2016 |work=On Location Vacations |date=January 20, 2016 |archive-date=January 26, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160126160347/http://www.onlocationvacations.com/2016/01/20/kong-skull-island-moves-hawaii-australia/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Simonot |first=Suzanne |title=Kong: Skull Island cast and crew wanted as filming continues |url=http://www.goldcoastbulletin.com.au/kong-skull-island-cast-and-crew-wanted-as-filming-continues/news-story/82f35fcfc2b77ca0543c07b123d507e6 |access-date=January 26, 2016 |work=Gold Coast Bulletin |date=January 24, 2016 |archive-date=February 1, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160201000909/http://www.goldcoastbulletin.com.au/kong-skull-island-cast-and-crew-wanted-as-filming-continues/news-story/82f35fcfc2b77ca0543c07b123d507e6 |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Influences==
Vogt-Roberts has cited several films that influenced ''Kong: Skull Island'':<ref name="fanfeb">{{cite web |url=http://www.fandango.com/movie-news/director-jordan-vogt-roberts-on-why-kong-skull-island-is-unlike-any-other-king-kong-movie-751932 |title=Director Jordan Vogt-Roberts On Why 'Kong: Skull Island' Is Unlike Any Other 'King Kong' Movie |last=Davis |first=Erik |work=Fandango |date=February 17, 2017 |access-date=February 17, 2017 |archive-date=February 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170218024039/http://www.fandango.com/movie-news/director-jordan-vogt-roberts-on-why-kong-skull-island-is-unlike-any-other-king-kong-movie-751932 |url-status=live }}</ref>

{{Blockquote
|text=If I were going to break it down for people, I'd say you obviously have ''[[Apocalypse Now]]'' and just the era of '70s filmmaking, with films like ''[[The Conversation]]'', too. Also, ''[[Platoon (film)|Platoon]]'' was an inspiration, and the South Korean film ''[[The Host (2006 film)|The Host]]'' as well. The entire ''[[Neon Genesis Evangelion]]'' series was a big influence. There's a huge anime and video game influence in my DNA, and I think it very much bred itself into this film.}}

Other inspirations include the South Korean films ''[[The Good, the Bad, the Weird]]'' and ''[[Oldboy (2003 film)|Oldboy]]'', plus video games like the ''[[List of Alien, Predator, and Alien vs. Predator games|Aliens]]'' series, ''[[The Legend of Zelda]]'' series, and ''[[Shadow of the Colossus]]''.<ref name="fanfeb" /><ref name="PlayList">{{cite web|url=https://theplaylist.net/influence-director-jordan-vogt-roberts-talks-inspirations-kong-skull-island-20170309/2/|title=Under The Influence: Director Jordan Vogt-Roberts Talks The Inspirations Behind 'Kong: Skull Island'|first=Rodrigo|last=Perez|work=[[Playlist.com]]|date=March 9, 2017|access-date=October 28, 2021|archive-date=October 28, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211028232753/https://theplaylist.net/influence-director-jordan-vogt-roberts-talks-inspirations-kong-skull-island-20170309/2/|url-status=live}}</ref> The film's opening scene where an American and a Japanese pilot are stranded on the same island was inspired by ''[[Hell in the Pacific]]'' (1968).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Perez |first=Rodrigo |date=2017-03-09 |title=Under The Influence: Director Jordan Vogt-Roberts Talks The Inspirations Behind 'Kong: Skull Island' - Page 2 of 2 |url=https://theplaylist.net/influence-director-jordan-vogt-roberts-talks-inspirations-kong-skull-island-20170309/ |access-date=2025-10-09 |website=The Playlist |language=en-US}}</ref> The animated works ''[[Spirited Away]]'' and ''[[Princess Mononoke]]'' by [[Hayao Miyazaki]] influenced the approach and design of the monsters in ''Kong: Skull Island'',<ref name="10things" /> as did [[List of Angels in Neon Genesis Evangelion#Sachiel|Sachiel]] from ''Neon Genesis Evangelion'', [[Cubone]] from ''[[Pokémon]]'', and the two-legged lizard from the original ''King Kong''.<ref name="fanfeb" /> The film also references the Italian horror movie ''[[Cannibal Holocaust]]'' when a giant spider impales a soldier with its leg.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://bloody-disgusting.com/news/3428083/yes-intentional-brutal-cannibal-holocaust-tribute-kong-skull-island/|title=Yes, There Was an Intentional (and Brutal) 'Cannibal Holocaust' Tribute in 'Kong: Skull Island'|first=John|last=Squires|publisher=[[Bloody Disgusting]]|date=13 March 2017|access-date=31 March 2023|archive-date=March 31, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230331113751/https://bloody-disgusting.com/news/3428083/yes-intentional-brutal-cannibal-holocaust-tribute-kong-skull-island/|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Music==
{{Main|Kong: Skull Island (soundtrack){{!}}''Kong: Skull Island'' (soundtrack)}}
[[Henry Jackman]] composed the score. Jackman blended '70s psychedelic guitars into the score to blend with the film's setting in the 1970s.<ref name="production notes">{{cite web |url=http://www.scifijapan.com/articles/2017/02/18/kong-skull-island-production-notes-and-high-res-photos/ |title=Kong: Skull Island Production Notes |work=SciFi Japan |date=February 18, 2017 |access-date=February 19, 2017 |archive-date=February 18, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170218192315/http://www.scifijapan.com/articles/2017/02/18/kong-skull-island-production-notes-and-high-res-photos/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> Vogt-Roberts wanted to use songs from the Vietnam era and a myriad of hits from then as it provides a "striking dichotomy, sets the tone and gives us great moments of fun."<ref name="production notes" /> The score was recorded at [[Associated Independent Recording#AIR Lyndhurst Hall - Hampstead, London (1991–present)|AIR Lyndhurst Studios]] with the [[London Voices]] and conducted by [[Gavin Greenaway]], with additional music by Alex Belcher, [[Halli Cauthery]], and [[Stephen Hilton]]. The soundtrack was digitally released in March 2017, through [[WaterTower Music]] and then later released in 2018 by [[Waxwork Records]] on a double LP.<ref>{{cite web |author=Anderton, Ethan |date=21 August 2018 |title=Cool Stuff: Henry Jackman's 'Kong: Skull Island' Score Gets a Lava Vinyl Soundtrack |url=https://www.slashfilm.com/cool-stuff-henry-jackmans-kong-skull-island-score-gets-a-lava-vinyl-soundtrack/ |access-date=14 August 2020 |location=/Film |archive-date=November 28, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201128211339/https://www.slashfilm.com/cool-stuff-henry-jackmans-kong-skull-island-score-gets-a-lava-vinyl-soundtrack/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Release==
===Merchandise===
The merchandise for the film was a [[Walmart]] exclusive in 2017. A large Kong figure was the main toy featuring a Jack Chapman with a missile launcher. In addition to Walmart selling the toys, Amazon.com sells them too. Also, two costumes for Kong were made and sold during [[Halloween]]. One of them is a standard costume, while the other was an inflatable Kong suit.

On April 7, 2017, Legendary announced a four-issue graphic novel series called ''Skull Island: The Birth of Kong''. Acting as both a prequel and sequel to the film, an adult Houston Brooks nearing retirement from Monarch in 2012 learns that his missing estranged son with San Lin, Aaron, led a team on a secret mission to Skull Island in the mid-1990s. During the mission, the team uncovered secrets of Kong's past and how he became the last of his kind.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://ew.com/movies/2017/04/07/birth-of-kong-comic-series-connects-skull-island/ |title='Birth of Kong' Comic Series Connects the Dots of 'Skull Island' – First Look |last=Snetiker |first=Marc |date=April 7, 2017 |website=EW.com |language=en |access-date=January 20, 2019 |archive-date=April 15, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190415114219/https://ew.com/movies/2017/04/07/birth-of-kong-comic-series-connects-skull-island/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Written by Arvid Nelson with interior and cover art by Mohammad "Zid" Yazid (issue No. 4 cover art done by Drew Johnson), the four-issue series was released between April 12 and November 21, 2017. On December 12, 2017, a paperback collection was released. A novelization by [[Tim Lebbon]] was released on March 14, 2017.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://thegeeksattic.com/kong-skull-island-novelization-review/ |title=Kong Skull Island Novelization Review |access-date=June 8, 2019 |date=December 29, 2017 |archive-date=June 8, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190608075553/http://thegeeksattic.com/kong-skull-island-novelization-review/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Theatrical===
''Kong: Skull Island'' was originally scheduled to be released on November 4, 2016, but was pushed back to March 10, 2017. The new release date coincided with the franchise's 84th anniversary. It was presented in [[70mm]] in select cinemas.<ref name="ReleaseTHR">{{cite news |last1=Ford |first1=Rebecca |title=Universal Pushes King Kong Film to 2017, Dates Great Wall Movie for 2016 |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/universal-pushes-king-kong-film-757353 |access-date=December 13, 2014 |work=The Hollywood Reporter |date=December 12, 2014 |archive-date=February 8, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150208170728/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/universal-pushes-king-kong-film-757353 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/markhughes/2017/03/06/kong-skull-island-delivers-king-sized-action-and-monster-thrills/ |title='Kong: Skull Island' Delivers King-Sized Action And Monster Thrills |first=Mark |last=Hughes |work=Forbes |access-date=March 6, 2017 |archive-date=March 6, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170306161216/https://www.forbes.com/sites/markhughes/2017/03/06/kong-skull-island-delivers-king-sized-action-and-monster-thrills/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The film premiered at the [[Empire, Leicester Square|Cineworld Empire Leicester Square]] in [[London]] on February 28, 2017.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.gettyimages.ca/event/the-european-premiere-of-kong-skull-island-arrivals-700012902#brie-larson-tom-hiddleston-and-samuel-l-jackson-attend-the-european-picture-id646342868|title=The European Premiere Of "Kong: Skull Island" – Arrivals Photos and Images {{!}} Getty Images|website=www.gettyimages.ca|language=en-gb|access-date=March 3, 2017|archive-date=June 2, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180602043817/https://www.gettyimages.ca/event/the-european-premiere-of-kong-skull-island-arrivals-700012902#brie-larson-tom-hiddleston-and-samuel-l-jackson-attend-the-european-picture-id646342868|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Home media===
''Kong: Skull Island'' was released on HD Digital on June 20, 2017, and on 4K Ultra HD, [[3D Blu-ray]], Blu-ray, and DVD on July 18, 2017.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.comingsoon.net/dvd/news/852109-kong-skull-island-blu-ray-details-and-box-art-revealed#/slide/1 |title=Kong: Skull Island Blu-ray Details and Box Art Revealed |last=Evry |first=Max |work=Coming Soon |date=May 24, 2017 |access-date=May 24, 2017 |archive-date=May 25, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170525011839/http://www.comingsoon.net/dvd/news/852109-kong-skull-island-blu-ray-details-and-box-art-revealed#/slide/1 |url-status=live }}</ref> The film debuted at the top of the NPD VideoScan First Alert sales chart and the dedicated Blu-ray chart for the week ending on July 23, 2017.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://variety.com/2017/digital/news/kong-skull-island-stomps-to-no-1-on-home-video-charts-1202508565/ |title='Kong: Skull Island' Stomps to No. 1 on Home-Video Charts |last=Latchem |first=John |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |date=July 27, 2017 |access-date=July 27, 2017 |archive-date=July 29, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170729220504/http://variety.com/2017/digital/news/kong-skull-island-stomps-to-no-1-on-home-video-charts-1202508565/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In the United States and Canada, the DVD earned $16.6 million and the Blu-ray earned $23.3 million, totaling $39.9 million in domestic video sales.<ref>{{cite the numbers |id=Kong-Skull-Island |title=Kong: Skull Island |access-date=February 19, 2021}}</ref>

==Reception==
===Box office===
''Kong: Skull Island'' grossed $168.1&nbsp;million in the United States and Canada and $402.8&nbsp;million in other territories for a worldwide gross of $570.9&nbsp;million.<ref name="BOM">{{cite Box Office Mojo |id=3731562 |title=Kong: Skull Island |access-date=February 19, 2021}}</ref> With a production budget of $185 million, with about $136 million more spent on international marketing costs, the film needed to make at least $450–500 million worldwide to [[break-even]].<ref name="THR" /><ref>{{cite web |url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-logan-weekend-box-office-get-out-1202040377/ |title=Sizing Up 'Kong: Skull Island's Weekend Domestic Opening |first=Anthony |last=D'Alessandro |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |date=March 11, 2017 |access-date=March 12, 2017 |archive-date=March 11, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170311173053/http://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-logan-weekend-box-office-get-out-1202040377/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://variety.com/2017/film/box-office/box-office-kong-skull-island-rules-with-mighty-61-million-debut-1202007236/ |title=Box Office: 'Kong: Skull Island' Rules With Mighty $61 Million Debut |first=Brent |last=Lang |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |access-date=March 12, 2017}}</ref>

In the United States and Canada, ''Kong: Skull Island'' was projected to gross $40–50&nbsp;million in its opening weekend, as well as a worldwide debut of $110–135&nbsp;million.<ref name="preview" /><ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/logan-box-office-opening-get-out-the-shack-1202035207/ |title='Logan' $85.3M Debut Breaks Records For Wolverine Series & Rated R Fare; Beats 'Fifty Shades' & 'Passion of the Christ' |first=Anthony |last=D'Alessandro |magazine=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |date=March 5, 2017 |access-date=March 6, 2017}}</ref> The film made $20.2&nbsp;million on its first day from 3,846 theaters, including $3.7&nbsp;million it made from Thursday night previews.<ref name="opening">{{cite web |url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-logan-weekend-box-office-get-out-1202040377/ |title='Kong: Skull Island' Conquering 'Logan' For Top Spot at B.O. With $53M – Midday Update |first=Anthony |last=D'Alessandro |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |access-date=March 10, 2017 |archive-date=March 10, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170310183814/http://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-logan-weekend-box-office-get-out-1202040377/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In total, the film earned a better-than-expected $61&nbsp;million on its opening weekend, defying the film's initial projection by 35%.<ref name="DDD">{{cite web |url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-beating-box-office-projections-logan-get-out-1202041809/ |title='Kong' Beats His Chest On Saturday: Weekend Opening Now At $61M – Sunday AM Update |first=Anthony |last=D'Alessandro |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |date=March 12, 2017 |access-date=March 12, 2017 |archive-date=March 12, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170312111607/http://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-beating-box-office-projections-logan-get-out-1202041809/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="THR">{{cite web |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/weekend-box-office-kong-skull-island-scales-61m-no-1-finish-985412 |title=Weekend Box Office: 'Kong: Skull Island' Scales $61M for No. 1 Finish |first=Pamela |last=McClintock |work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |date=March 12, 2017 |access-date=March 12, 2017 |archive-date=March 12, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170312165922/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/weekend-box-office-kong-skull-island-scales-61m-no-1-finish-985412 |url-status=live }}</ref> It made $7.6 million from 382 theaters in IMAX, representing 12.5% of the film's entire opening weekend.<ref name="DDD" /> In its second weekend, the film grossed $27.8&nbsp;million (a drop of 54.4%), finishing second at the box office behind newcomer ''[[Beauty and the Beast (2017 film)|Beauty and the Beast]]''.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/beauty-and-the-beast-weekend-box-office-selling-out-1202045224/ |title='Beauty and the Beast' $174.8M Opening Sparks Moviegoing Explosion; Pic Could Conquer 'Rogue One' & 'Dark Knight' |first=Anthony |last=D'Alessandro |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |date=March 21, 2017 |access-date=March 22, 2017 |archive-date=March 20, 2017 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20170320230239/http://deadline.com/2017/03/beauty-and-the-beast-weekend-box-office-selling-out-1202045224/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

Internationally, the film debuted with $85.1&nbsp;million from 20,900 screens in 65 markets. It opened in every market except Japan and China. The film scored the fourth-biggest March release with $4.8&nbsp;million from 672 theaters in IMAX (the second biggest without China in it).<ref name="INTL">{{cite web |url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-logan-dogs-purpose-china-weekend-international-box-office-results-1202041853/ |title='Kong' King In $81.6M Offshore Bow; 'Logan' Leaps To $437M Global – Intl Box Office |first=Nancy |last=Tartaglione |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |date=March 12, 2017 |access-date=March 13, 2017 |archive-date=March 13, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170313020446/http://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-logan-dogs-purpose-china-weekend-international-box-office-results-1202041853/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The biggest openings came from the [[United Kingdom]], [[Republic of Ireland|Ireland]] ($7.6 million); [[South Korea]] ($7.4 million); [[Russia]] ($6.2 million); [[Mexico]] ($5.7 million); [[France]] ($4.1 million); [[Taiwan]] ($3.6 million); [[Australia]] ($3.6 million); [[Brazil]] ($3.4 million), [[Germany]] ($3.4 million); [[Malaysia]] ($2.65 million); [[India]] ($2.4 million); [[Spain]] ($1.6 million), and [[Italy]] ($1.6 million). In [[Vietnam]] (where the film was primarily shot and set), it scored the biggest opening of all time there with $2.5&nbsp;million; this was the week after a huge model of the primate outside the theater caught on fire at the film's premiere.<ref name="THR" /><ref name="INTL" /> The film would eventually open in China with $71.6 million (its largest international market) and $3.5 million in Japan, where the film was released as ''King Kong: Giant God of Skull Island'' (''Kingu Kongu: Dokurotou no Kyoshin'').<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.scifijapan.com/articles/2016/11/12/kong-skull-island-japanese-trailer-and-logo/ |title=Kong: Skull Island Japanese Trailer and Logo |access-date=November 29, 2017 |work=Scifijapan.com |archive-date=October 7, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171007185118/http://www.scifijapan.com/articles/2016/11/12/kong-skull-island-japanese-trailer-and-logo/ |url-status=live }}</ref> After its overseas run, the film would gross US$400 million internationally.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.boxofficemojo.com/movies/?page=intl&id=legendary2016.htm |title=Kong: Skull Island |access-date=April 27, 2017 |work=[[Box Office Mojo]] |archive-date=April 11, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180411163746/http://www.boxofficemojo.com/movies/?page=intl&id=legendary2016.htm |url-status=live }}</ref> It is the second highest-grossing film in the [[Monsterverse]] to date.

===Critical response===
''Kong: Skull Island'' received generally positive reviews from critics.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://collider.com/kong-skull-island-fan-reviews/ |title='Kong: Skull Island': What Did You Think? |last=Goldberg |first=Matt |work=Collider |date=March 10, 2017 |access-date=March 15, 2017 |archive-date=March 13, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170313212412/http://collider.com/kong-skull-island-fan-reviews/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/scottmendelson/2017/03/13/kong-skull-island-four-lessons-for-justice-league-and-the-dc-films-franchise/ |title='Kong: Skull Island': Four Lessons For 'Justice League' And The DC Films Franchise |last=Mendelson |first=Scott |work=Forbes |date=March 13, 2017 |access-date=March 15, 2017 |archive-date=March 13, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170313210239/https://www.forbes.com/sites/scottmendelson/2017/03/13/kong-skull-island-four-lessons-for-justice-league-and-the-dc-films-franchise/ |url-status=live }}</ref> {{Rotten Tomatoes prose|75|6.5|390|Offering exhilarating eye candy, solid acting, and a fast-paced story, ''Kong: Skull Island'' earns its spot in the movie monster's mythos without ever matching up to the classic original.|ref=yes|access-date=October 14, 2026}} [[Metacritic]], which uses a [[Weighted arithmetic mean|weighted average]], assigned the film a score of 62 out of 100, based on 50 critics, indicating "generally favorable" reviews.<ref name="Metacritic">{{cite web |title=''Kong: Skull Island'' |url=https://www.metacritic.com/movie/kong-skull-island |website=[[Metacritic]] |publisher=[[Fandom (website)#Fandom, Inc.|Fandom, Inc.]] |access-date=October 14, 2026 |archive-url= |archive-date= |url-status=}}</ref> Audiences polled by [[CinemaScore]] gave the film an average grade of "B+" on an A+ to F scale.<ref name="CinemaScore">{{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/CinemaScore/status/840452223805095936 |title=''Kong: Skull Island'' |publisher=[[CinemaScore]] on [[Twitter]] |date=March 10, 2017 |access-date=April 10, 2017 |archive-date=June 2, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180602043816/https://twitter.com/CinemaScore/status/840452223805095936 |url-status=live }}</ref> Audiences surveyed by [[PostTrak]] gave the film an overall positive score of 80%, and 60% of the audience would definitely recommend it.<ref>{{cite web|date=March 11, 2017|last=D'Alessandro|first=Anthony|title=Sizing Up 'Kong: Skull Island's Weekend Domestic Opening|url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-logan-weekend-box-office-get-out-1202040377/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|access-date=November 12, 2023|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-date=October 21, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231021085547/https://deadline.com/2017/03/kong-skull-island-logan-weekend-box-office-get-out-1202040377/}}</ref>

[[Michael Phillips (critic)|Michael Phillips]] of ''[[The Chicago Tribune]]'' lauded the film, giving it three-and-a-half stars out of four: "I saw little in [Vogt-Roberts'] [[The Kings of Summer|first feature]] to indicate the deftness and buoyant spirit he brings to ''Skull Island''. This time, the money's on the screen, but it bought a really good movie, too."<ref name="CinemaScore2">{{cite news |url=https://www.chicagotribune.com/entertainment/movies/sc-kong-skull-island-mov-rev-0307-20170307-column.html |title='Kong: Skull Island' review: Big budget buys dazzling effects and a really good movie too |newspaper=[[The Chicago Tribune]] |date=March 8, 2017 |access-date=May 30, 2017 |archive-date=May 25, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170525091103/http://www.chicagotribune.com/entertainment/movies/sc-kong-skull-island-mov-rev-0307-20170307-column.html |url-status=live }}{{rating|3.5|4}}</ref> Mike Ryan of ''[[Uproxx]]'' gave the film a positive review, noting, "''Kong: Skull Island'' is still a hoot. It was a movie that was not at all on my radar as something I was dying to see and yet I had way too much fun watching it. I just wished it had embraced its craziness just a little bit more. (But, yes, there's still plenty of crazy to go around.)"<ref>{{cite web |last=Ryan |first=Mike |url=http://uproxx.com/movies/kong-skull-island-review/ |title='Kong: Skull Island' Is Ridiculous Fun |website=Uproxx |date=March 2, 2017 |access-date=March 2, 2017 |archive-date=March 3, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170303003754/http://uproxx.com/movies/kong-skull-island-review/ |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Todd McCarthy]] of ''[[The Hollywood Reporter]]'' gave the film a positive review as well, stating that "all the requisite elements are served up here in ideal proportion, and the time just flies by, which can rarely be said for films of this nature."<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/review/kong-skull-island-review-982156 |title='Kong: Skull Island': Film Review |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |date=March 2, 2017 |access-date=April 17, 2020 |archive-date=February 13, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200213201423/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/review/kong-skull-island-review-982156 |url-status=live }}</ref> Kyle Anderson of ''[[Nerdist News]]'' found the film entertaining but flawed, saying, "It's certainly not a perfect movie, and a lot of the characters feel like sketches more than fully-fledged people, but it roars along enjoyably from start to finish."<ref>{{cite web |url=https://archive.nerdist.com/kong-skull-island-is-big-raucous-monster-fun-review/ |title=KONG: SKULL ISLAND IS BIG, RAUCOUS MONSTER FUN (REVIEW) |access-date=March 3, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170314143224/http://nerdist.com/kong-skull-island-is-big-raucous-monster-fun-review/ |archive-date=March 14, 2017 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Conversely, [[Peter Bradshaw]] of ''[[The Guardian]]'' awarded the film one out of five stars. In his negative review, he described the movie as a "fantastically muddled and exasperatingly dull quasi-update of the King Kong story."<ref>{{cite web |last=Bradshaw |first=Peter |url=https://www.theguardian.com/film/2017/mar/02/kong-skull-island-tom-hiddleston-review-only-de-evolution-can-explain-this-zestless-mashup |title=Kong: Skull Island review – only de-evolution can explain this zestless mashup |website=The Guardian |date=March 3, 2017 |access-date=March 3, 2017 |archive-date=May 29, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180529173717/https://www.theguardian.com/film/2017/mar/02/kong-skull-island-tom-hiddleston-review-only-de-evolution-can-explain-this-zestless-mashup |url-status=live }}{{rating|1|5}}</ref> Matthew Lickona of ''[[The San Diego Reader]]'' also gave the film one out of five stars, writing: "It's fun to watch [the monsters] in action, but on the human side, the film is clumsily written, over-cast and underacted, with only frustrated soldier Samuel L. Jackson striking the right tone of crazy amid the chaos."<ref>{{cite web |last=Lickona |first=Matthew |url=https://www.sandiegoreader.com/movies/kong-skull-island/ |title=KONG: SKULL ISLAND 1.0 STARS |website=The San Diego Reader |date=March 2017 |access-date=May 30, 2017 |archive-date=March 17, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170317164605/http://www.sandiegoreader.com/movies/kong-skull-island/ |url-status=live }}{{rating|1|5}}</ref> Chris Klimek of ''[[NPR]]'' mentions how "''Kong'' is at its mediocre best when it pretends to be a nature documentary about Skull Island's bizarro flora and fauna," but lamented how "every time the movie threatens to get interesting, one of its hordes of ersatz, non-animated characters shows up and starts talking again."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Klimek |first1=Chris |title=In The Forgettable 'Kong: Skull Island,' A Great Cast, Cast Aside |url=https://www.npr.org/2017/03/09/518778017/in-the-forgettable-kong-skull-island-a-great-cast-cast-aside |website=NPR.org |language=en |date=March 9, 2017 |access-date=April 5, 2018 |archive-date=June 22, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170622004959/http://www.npr.org/2017/03/09/518778017/in-the-forgettable-kong-skull-island-a-great-cast-cast-aside |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Anthony Lane]] of ''[[The New Yorker]]'' noted that what the film "yearns to be, is a pop-culture ''[[Apocalypse Now]]'', with the human foe removed, the political parable toned down, and the gonzo elements jacked up."<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Lane |first1=Anthony |title=The Current Cinema: "Kong: Skull Island" |url=https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2017/03/13/kong-skull-island-and-raw |magazine=The New Yorker |publisher=Condé Nast |date=March 13, 2017}}</ref> J.R. Jones questioned the film's setting, saying "this ''[[Jurassic Park (film)|Jurassic Park]]'' knockoff takes place neither in the Depression era, which gave us the original ''[[King Kong (1933 film)|King Kong]]'', nor in the present, when satellite photos would surely alert us to the existence of a 100-foot gorilla. Instead—and for no reason I can fathom, except perhaps the classic-rock tunes desired for the soundtrack—the story takes place in 1973, when the Vietnam war is winding down and President Nixon is being driven from office."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Jones |first1=J.R. |title=Kong: Skull Island |url=https://www.chicagoreader.com/chicago/kong-skull-island/Film?oid=25527309 |website=Chicago Reader |date=March 9, 2017 |language=en |access-date=September 24, 2017 |archive-date=September 1, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170901224913/https://www.chicagoreader.com/chicago/kong-skull-island/Film?oid=25527309 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Regarding Larson's role in the film, Ann Hornaday of ''[[The Washington Post]]'' stated that Larson "serves as a cautionary poster girl for aspiring actresses everywhere: One year you're winning an Oscar for a sensitive, skillfully layered performance in an emotionally demanding drama; the next, you're widening your eyes and gasping your way through a great big monkey movie."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hornaday |first1=Ann |title=Hollywood ageism punishes actresses, but the art house offers some hope |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/lifestyle/style/hollywood-ageism-punishes-actress-but-the-art-house-offers-some-hope/2017/03/09/ce7e0e24-040c-11e7-ad5b-d22680e18d10_story.html |date=March 9, 2017 |access-date=March 13, 2017 |archive-date=March 10, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170310103039/https://www.washingtonpost.com/lifestyle/style/hollywood-ageism-punishes-actress-but-the-art-house-offers-some-hope/2017/03/09/ce7e0e24-040c-11e7-ad5b-d22680e18d10_story.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Michael Salfino of ''[[The Wall Street Journal]]'' remarked, "a starring role in a popcorn movie on the heels of a passion project can open up an actor to ridicule."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-her-oscar-brie-larson-stars-withking-kong-1489008626|title=After Her Oscar, Brie Larson Stars With…King Kong?|first=Michael|last=Salfino|work=The Wall Street Journal|date=March 8, 2017|access-date=December 12, 2020|url-status=live|archive-date=December 13, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201213044058/https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-her-oscar-brie-larson-stars-withking-kong-1489008626}}</ref>

